    "JurisdictionSpecifics": "Texas. Manslaughter under Texas Penal Code § 19.04 requires proof beyond a reasonable doubt that the defendant recklessly caused the death of another. Murder under § 19.02 requires proof of intentional or knowing causation, or felony murder. The State charged both defendants with Manslaughter (reckless) and alternatively with Criminally Negligent Homicide (§ 19.05). The defendants claim they were acting under orders from their Training Sergeant during a sanctioned disciplinary exercise. The central question is not whether the defendants caused the death — they admit they did — but whether they acted under orders and whether their conduct was reckless or merely negligent. The Training Sergeant denies giving any order for physical discipline.",
