        {
            "FileName": "Former Cadet Testimony - Pattern of Hazing.pdf",
            "FilePath": "",
            "Summary": "Testimony from three former Bexar County Police Academy cadets who graduated in the three classes prior to Oakes\u0027s. All three testified under subpoena (they did not volunteer — they were reluctant witnesses). CADET ONE (graduated 2024): Describes being woken at 2:00 AM, dragged to the common room by senior cadets, and having his head held in a toilet while being screamed at for \u0027disrespecting the uniform.\u0027 States Sergeant Cross walked through the common room during the incident, looked at what was happening, and said \u0027carry on\u0027 before returning to his office. CADET TWO (graduated 2023): Describes being beaten with a soap-filled sock (\u0027the Code Red special\u0027) by senior cadets after Cross told them to \u0027deal with his attitude problem.\u0027 States Cross later told him \u0027you earned that\u0027 and that the hazing \u0027made you a better officer.\u0027 CADET THREE (graduated 2023): Describes being ordered to do pushups on broken glass from a dropped mirror as punishment for breaking formation. States Cross was present and did not intervene. CROSS-EXAMINATION: The prosecution established that none of these former cadets filed formal complaints at the time. Each said they \u0027didn\u0027t want to be labeled a rat\u0027 and \u0027just wanted to graduate.\u0027 The prosecution also established that none of the three witnessed the Oakes incident and that their testimony goes to \u0027culture\u0027 rather than the specific crime charged.",
            "AdmittedAt": "2025-07-03T14:00:00",
