        {
            "FileName": "Video - Academy Surveillance Footage (Hallway).mp4",
            "FilePath": "",
            "Summary": "Surveillance camera footage from the hallway outside the Training Sergeant\u0027s office at the Bexar County Police Academy barracks. The footage is timestamped and shows: (1) 01:14:32 AM — Kowalski and Reyes enter Sergeant Cross\u0027s office. (2) 01:22:47 AM — Kowalski and Reyes exit Cross\u0027s office. Both appear tense. Kowalski is gesturing; Reyes is nodding. The interaction lasts approximately 8 minutes. (3) 01:55:18 AM — Kowalski and Reyes walk down the hallway toward the bunk room. (4) 01:56:41 AM — Kowalski and Reyes return, carrying Oakes between them. Oakes appears limp/unconscious. His head is hanging down and his feet are dragging. (5) 01:58:02 AM — They enter the bunk room with Oakes. (6) 01:59:30 AM — Kowalski and Reyes exit the bunk room and return to their own bunks. PROSECUTION NOTE: The video shows the defendants carrying an obviously unconscious Oakes — and then just going back to bed. No attempt to seek help. No checking to see if he was breathing. They left him to die. DEFENSE NOTE: The video does NOT show what happened in the common room — only the hallway. It shows the aftermath, which the defendants admit. They do not dispute that they panicked afterward. The video does not prove what level of force was used or whether they intended harm.",
            "AdmittedAt": "2025-07-01T10:00:00",
            "ExhibitNumber": 10,
            "EvidenceStrength": 0.58,
            "IsDiscoveryComplete": true,
            "ClerkNotes": "Prosecution exhibit. The video of them carrying Oakes\u0027s limp body and then just going to bed is HIGHLY prejudicial. It looks terrible. The defense\u0027s counter — \u0027we admit we panicked, that\u0027s not the crime\u0027 — is legally correct but emotionally weak. Jurors will see that footage and feel anger. The 8-minute meeting with Cross corroborates BOTH sides: the defense says Cross gave the order; the prosecution says Cross gave a lawful counseling instruction.",
